course: dictionary
lesson: 13524
title: Words for tiny changes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some changes happen so slowly that you cannot catch them while they happen. The word for this is imperceptibly. «The tree grew taller imperceptibly, a little each day.» You cannot see the tree grow from minute to minute, but you know it grew because the difference shows over time. Imperceptibly means so slowly or slightly that you cannot notice it happening.
explain: The word can also mean too small to see, hear or feel. «He nodded imperceptibly, so only Mia noticed.» The nod was so small that most people missed it. Look for clues like «slowly», «a little each day» or «so small» in the sentence: they point to the meaning.
explain: Try a swap to check. Put «slowly» or «so small you miss it» in place of imperceptibly. «The sky grew darker imperceptibly as the sun set» still makes sense with «slowly», so you have the right meaning.
fact: Imperceptibly means so slowly or slightly that you cannot notice it happening.
fact: It is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens.
fact: Many changes happen imperceptibly: plants grow, the hour hand moves, mountains wear down and continents drift.
fact: «The light faded imperceptibly at dusk» means the light got dimmer so gradually that you did not notice when.
fact: Useful phrases: change imperceptibly, nod imperceptibly, imperceptibly slowly.
exercise: «The hour hand moved imperceptibly across the clock.» How did the hour hand move? | *So slowly you could not see it move | Backwards | Very fast, with a bang | Only when someone pushed it
exercise: «Her friend nodded imperceptibly, so the teacher did not see.» What does imperceptibly mean? | Angrily and fast | Happily, with a big smile | Very loudly and clearly | *So small that others hardly noticed
exercise: Which change happens imperceptibly? | A thunderclap | A cup falling off a table | A firework bursting | *A mountain slowly wearing down
test: Continents drift imperceptibly over millions of years. What does imperceptibly tell you about the drift? | In a loud way | Only in winter | Very fast and sudden | *So slowly that we cannot notice it
test: «The light changed imperceptibly.» Which phrase means the same as imperceptibly here? | *So gradually you cannot notice | Loudly and quickly | All at once | With a big crash
exam: Which sentence shows something that happens imperceptibly? | The door slammed shut | The thunder crashed across the sky | The crowd cheered loudly | *The plant grew a little each day, too slowly to see
